  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant directions: arc melting and water quenching can retain metastable phase arrangements; composition and processing can create Laves-containing or other dual-phase HEAs; and fine phase decomposition can reduce saturation magnetization while increasing coercivity in a magnetic HEA. They also show temperature-dependent magnetism in fcc/hcp transition-metal HEAs. However, none identifies the FeCoNiTi fcc/C14 combination, the Fe/Co/Ni–Ti antiferromagnetic sublattice coupling, the phase-specific 168/214/1084 K transitions, or the orbital-moment/spin-canting-assisted domain-wall-pinning mechanism. Thus the literature points toward quenched multiphase magnetic-HEA design, but selecting the specific composition, C14 comparison alloy, and mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
